@startuml
!include style.iuml
' DFD level 0 (context diagram), Yourdon/DeMarco notation:
' circle = process, rectangle = external entity (terminator),
' dashed rectangle = optional external entity, labelled arrow = data flow.
' System boundary = process 0 = the whole SmartExam system (WPF desktop client
' with its lockdown, React web panel, ASP.NET Core API), as in the use-case
' diagram. The lab PC the student sits at is the student's side of the boundary.
skinparam defaultFontSize 16
skinparam ArrowFontSize 16
skinparam nodesep 30
skinparam ranksep 50
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam rectangle<<entity>> {
  BorderThickness 2
  RoundCorner 0
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}
skinparam usecase {
  BorderColor #333333
  BorderThickness 2
  BackgroundColor #F2F2F2
  FontSize 16
}
skinparam rectangle<<optional>> {
  RoundCorner 0
  BorderStyle dashed
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}
hide stereotype
left to right direction

rectangle "Student" <<entity>> as STU
rectangle "Admin /\nSuperAdmin" <<entity>> as ADM
rectangle "Teacher" <<entity>> as TEA
rectangle "Invigilator" <<entity>> as INV
rectangle "LLM grader\n(Groq / Gemini;\noptional, off)" <<optional>> as LLM
rectangle "Email server\n(SMTP)" <<entity>> as SMTP

usecase "**0**\nSmartExam\n(desktop client,\nweb panel, API)" as P0

STU --> P0 : credentials, PC hardware\nIDs, start, answers,\nsubmit; activity on the\nlab PC (apps, keys, USB,\nmonitors); screen,\nwebcam image
P0 --> STU : sign-in result, exam\nlist, questions, receipt\nhash; lockdown,\nwarnings, extra time,\nunlock; results,\nviolation history,\nperformance,\nnotifications (web\nportal)

ADM --> P0 : users, roles, binding\nreset; departments,\ncourses, labs,\nworkstations
ADM <-- P0 : audit log and chain\nstatus, system analytics

P0 <-- TEA : exam settings,\nattendance CSV, seats,\ninvigilators,\nannouncements; warn,\nextend, unlock,\nforce-submit, incident;\naccept / override,\nreport request
TEA <-- P0 : live status, timeline,\nscreenshots; suggested\nmarks, similarity\nmatrix; PDF / Excel /\nevidence-ZIP reports

P0 <-- INV : warn, extend, unlock,\nforce-submit, incident\n(assigned exams only)
INV <-- P0 : live status, timeline,\nscreenshots

P0 ..> LLM : theory answer, model\nanswer, rubric keywords;\ncode test results
LLM ..> P0 : suggested mark, code\nsummary

P0 --> SMTP : exam schedule, grade and\nannouncement emails
@enduml
